Caelestia lib: Qt 6.8 compatibility patch
=========================================

Applies to: caelestia lib pinned at d8f3b72b7bffa22ace30595c3190a9f8cedb7e44
Applied by: install.sh, stage_lib (idempotent, skipped when already applied)

The pinned lib commit uses four Qt 6.9-only APIs, so it does not compile
with the Qt 6.8.2 shipped by Parrot OS (Debian 13). This patch replaces
each use with the equivalent Qt 6.8 API. Every replacement also exists
in Qt 6.9, so the patched sources still build on newer Qt.

1. src/config/theme.cpp (2 spots)
   QString + QStringView operator+ is Qt 6.9. Use QString + QString
   via QStringView::toString().
2. src/screenshot/image.cpp
   QImage::flipped(Qt::Horizontal) is Qt 6.9. Use mirrored(true, false).
3. src/screenshot/screenshot.cpp
   Same QStringView concatenation fix as 1.
4. src/theme/theme.cpp
   QString::arg(int, 2, 16, u'0') is ambiguous on Qt 6.8. Pass QChar(u'0').

Proven on Parrot Security 7.4, Qt 6.8.2: lib builds and installs, and the
full installer plus verify.sh pass with this patch applied.

diff --git a/src/config/theme.cpp b/src/config/theme.cpp
index 6a120af..bb1f39d 100644
--- a/src/config/theme.cpp
+++ b/src/config/theme.cpp
@@ -10,11 +10,11 @@ ConfigTheme::ConfigTheme(Config* config)
     : m_config(config) {}
 
 bool ConfigTheme::targetEnabled(QStringView target) const {
-    return m_config->value(u"theme.targets."_s + target, true).toBool();
+    return m_config->value(u"theme.targets."_s + target.toString(), true).toBool();
 }
 
 void ConfigTheme::setTargetEnabled(QStringView target, bool enabled) const {
-    m_config->setValue(u"theme.targets."_s + target, enabled);
+    m_config->setValue(u"theme.targets."_s + target.toString(), enabled);
 }
 
 QString ConfigTheme::iconTheme() const {
diff --git a/src/screenshot/image.cpp b/src/screenshot/image.cpp
index 5fdecb8..4df62f6 100644
--- a/src/screenshot/image.cpp
+++ b/src/screenshot/image.cpp
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ QImage applyTransform(const QImage& image, uint32_t transform) {
     const auto rotation = static_cast<int>(transform & 3u) * 90;
 
     const auto result = rotation != 0 ? image.transformed(QTransform().rotate(rotation)) : image;
-    return flipped ? result.flipped(Qt::Horizontal) : result;
+    return flipped ? result.mirrored(true, false) : result;
 }
 
 QImage composite(const QRect& region, const QList<QRect>& geometries, const QList<QImage>& parts) {
